From: Campaign Worker <>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:13:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Accept explicit function arguments for scope giv and calls

The CLI validator omitted these implemented commands and rejected the documented FILE.c giv FUNC form. Checked validation directly and ran giv on the ranking routine to expose its counter-elimination decision.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1 Sol (Codex) <noreply@openai.com>
---
 tools/scope/scope.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/scope/scope.py b/tools/scope/scope.py
index 3be54e049..ba9e12ce2 100644
--- a/tools/scope/scope.py
+++ b/tools/scope/scope.py
@@ -5324,7 +5324,7 @@ def validate_cli(args):
     elif rest and rest[0] == "pins":
         if len([a for a in rest if a != "--all"]) > 2:
             cli_error("FILE.c pins [FUNC] [--all]")
-    elif any(a in rest for a in ("probe", "shape", "frame", "hoist", "spill", "pre")):
+    elif any(a in rest for a in ("probe", "shape", "frame", "hoist", "spill", "pre", "giv", "calls")):
         if len(rest) > 2:
             cli_error("FILE.c COMMAND [FUNC]")
     elif len(rest) > 1:
